.TH GPWEBCAM 1 "2026-10-07" "gpwebcam" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gpwebcam \- use a GoPro connected over USB as a Linux webcam
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gpwebcam run
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B gpwebcam start
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B gpwebcam config
.RI [ setting " [" value ]]
.br
.B gpwebcam record
.RB [ start | stop ]
.br
.B gpwebcam launch
.br
.B gpwebcam doctor
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B gpwebcam list
.br
.B gpwebcam version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gpwebcam
starts a GoPro's webcam mode through the Open GoPro HTTP API and writes
its video into a v4l2loopback device, which browsers, Zoom, OBS and other
V4L2 applications use as a camera named
.BR GoPro .
It runs as the logged-in user and needs no root.
.PP
While no camera sends video, gpwebcam writes a placeholder picture that
says why and names the camera model, so applications keep listing the
camera. Applications see the device by its label, GoPro by default; the
label is fixed when the module is loaded.
.PP
.B gpwebcam run
shows an icon in the desktop's system tray (StatusNotifierItem). Its menu
shows the camera's state and changes the settings: camera mode, field of
view, resolution, hardware decoding and notifications.
.PP
By default the camera streams on demand: gpwebcam starts it when an
application turns on the video of the device, and stops it 15 seconds
after the last one turned it off. v4l2loopback reports this to gpwebcam.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Keep running: wait for a camera, stream it while it is connected, and show
the placeholder while it is not, with the tray icon. This is what the
systemd user service
.B gpwebcam.service
runs. It applies a changed setting within about 2 seconds: a new field of
view or decoder restarts the camera; a new resolution applies once no
application uses the camera, because applications keep the frame size they
started with.
.TP
.B start
Stream one camera session and exit when it ends.
.TP
.BR config " [\fIsetting\fR [\fIvalue\fR]]"
Without arguments, print every setting; with a setting, print its value;
with a value too, change it. The settings are
.B camera
(demand, always, off),
.B res
(1080, 720),
.B fov
(wide, narrow, superview, linear),
.B hwdec
(auto, none),
.B notify
(on, off) and
.B tray
(on, off). The tray menu changes the same file.
.TP
.BR record " [" start | stop ]
Start or stop a recording in the running
.BR "gpwebcam run" ,
as the tray menu does; without an argument, say whether it records. The
camera's video goes as it is, without decoding, into a Matroska file in
~/Videos/gpwebcam, named by its start time. While recording, the camera
streams even when no application uses it; unplugging it or turning the
camera mode off ends the recording.
.TP
.B launch
Start the user service gpwebcam.service, as
.B systemctl \-\-user start gpwebcam
does, and say in a notification whether it started or was running
already. The GoPro Webcam entry in the application menu runs it.
.TP
.B doctor
Check ffmpeg, the v4l2loopback module and device, the service, the
settings, the camera's connection, the firewall and the system tray, and
print what to fix. Reads the camera's
state but changes nothing. Exits with status 1 if a check fails.
.TP
.B list
List the network interfaces of connected GoPro cameras.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH OPTIONS
.B run
and
.B start
take these options, except
.BR \-camera ,
.B \-record\-dir
and
.BR \-tray ,
which only
.B run
has;
.B doctor
takes -ffmpeg, -iface, -video-nr, -device-label, -port and -http-timeout.
-camera, -res, -fov, -hwdec, -notify and -tray override the settings file;
without them the file applies.
.TP
.BI \-res " 1080|720"
Resolution of the stream. Default 1080.
.TP
.BI \-fov " wide|narrow|superview|linear"
Field of view. Default linear.
.TP
.BI \-device\-label " label"
card_label of the v4l2loopback device to write to. Default GoPro.
.TP
.BI \-video\-nr " n"
Write to /dev/video\fIn\fR instead of finding the device by label.
Default \-1, which means: find it by label.
.TP
.BI \-iface " name"
GoPro network interface. Needed only when several cameras are connected.
.TP
.BI \-port " port"
UDP port the camera streams to, 1024 to 65535. Default 8554.
.TP
.BI \-ffmpeg " path"
ffmpeg executable. Default ffmpeg from PATH.
.TP
.BI \-hwdec " auto|none"
Hardware decoding. auto decodes on the GPU through VAAPI when ffmpeg can
open a VAAPI device at start, and on the CPU otherwise; after two sessions
in a row without video it switches to the CPU for good. none always decodes
on the CPU. Default auto.
.TP
.BI \-notify= bool
Show desktop notifications through notify-send. Default true.
.TP
.BI \-tray= bool
Show the tray icon. Default true.
.TP
.BI \-record\-dir " folder"
Folder for recordings, an absolute path. Default ~/Videos/gpwebcam. The
packaged unit lets the service write to ~/Videos only; another folder also
needs ReadWritePaths in a drop-in for the unit.
.TP
.BI \-camera " demand|always|off"
When the camera streams: while an application uses the device, whenever it
is connected, or never. Only for
.BR run ;
default demand.
.TP
.BI \-dhcp\-wait " duration"
How long to wait for the camera to give the computer an IPv4 address.
Default 30s.
.TP
.BI \-connect\-wait " duration"
How long to wait for the camera's HTTP server to answer. Default 20s.
.TP
.BI \-http\-timeout " duration"
Timeout of each request to the camera. Default 5s (3s for doctor).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/gpwebcam.service
The user service. Enable it with
.BR "systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now gpwebcam.service" .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/modprobe.d/99-gpwebcam.conf
v4l2loopback options: /dev/video42 labelled GoPro, and a second device for
OBS Virtual Camera. A file with the same name in /etc/modprobe.d replaces it.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/modules-load.d/gpwebcam.conf
Loads v4l2loopback at boot.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gpwebcam/settings.json
The settings, written by the tray menu and
.BR "gpwebcam config" ;
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gpwebcam
when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is set.
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/gpwebcam.desktop
The GoPro Webcam entry in the application menu.
.TP
.I ~/Videos/gpwebcam
Recordings.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/gpwebcam/control.sock
The socket through which
.B gpwebcam record
talks to the running service; only the user can open it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success or when stopped by SIGINT or SIGTERM, 1 on an error or when a
.B doctor
check fails.
.SH EXAMPLES
Change the field of view; the running service applies it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gpwebcam config fov wide
.fi
.RE
.PP
Give the service an option that is not a setting:
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemctl \-\-user edit gpwebcam.service
.fi
.RE
.PP
and set
.PP
.RS
.nf
[Service]
ExecStart=
ExecStart=/usr/bin/gpwebcam run \-port 8555
.fi
.RE
.PP
Follow the log:
.PP
.RS
.nf
journalctl \-\-user \-u gpwebcam \-f
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
Only one application at a time can use a V4L2 camera; a second one gets
"Device or resource busy". v4l2loopback enforces this since version 0.14. On the camera, Preferences > Connections > USB
Connection must be GoPro Connect, not MTP.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR modprobe.d (5),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
https://github.com/darkodemic/gpwebcam
